WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.937 --> 00:00:17.459
in our freezer was melting because we still had no electricity.

2
00:00:18.479 --> 00:00:21.200
My friends and I were almost melting in the heat too.

3
00:00:22.241 --> 00:00:25.262
But we hadn't earned enough money to go to the movies.

4
00:00:27.803 --> 00:00:29.804
I guess my mom felt sorry for us.

5
00:00:30.988 --> 00:00:34.450
"I'll pay for everyone's movie tickets," she said.

6
00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:38.092
"You guys can use the money you earned to buy some snacks."

7
00:00:41.394 --> 00:00:42.774
We took a bus to the movies.

8
00:00:45.976 --> 00:00:46.857
And guess what.

9
00:00:47.497 --> 00:00:50.639
The air conditioner on the bus was broken too!

10
00:00:50.659 --> 00:00:56.422
"It seems like the whole city blew a fuse," said Molly.

11
00:00:56.442 --> 00:01:01.444
"I hope the air conditioner at the movies is working," said Josh.

12
00:01:03.765 --> 00:01:05.945
It was nice and cool in the movie theater.

13
00:01:06.926 --> 00:01:09.106
In fact, it was almost too cold.

14
00:01:10.387 --> 00:01:13.147
The movie was called Woolly's Wild Winter.

15
00:01:14.228 --> 00:01:16.228
It was about a girl and her dog, Woolly.

16
00:01:17.189 --> 00:01:21.090
They lived in a cabin in Alaska where there was lots of snow and ice.

17
00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:25.111
Pretty soon I was so cold that I was almost shivering!

18
00:01:26.251 --> 00:01:29.732
But when we got outside after the movie, it was hotter than ever.

19
00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:37.703
While we waited for the bus, Caswell kept jumping from one foot to the other.

20
00:01:37.724 --> 00:01:42.447
"Caswell, stop jumping around," said Molly.

21
00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:46.010
"It makes me hot just to look at you."

22
00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:51.134
"But I have to keep jumping," said Caswell.

23
00:01:51.154 --> 00:01:56.299
"The sidewalk is so hot, it burns the bottom of my shoes."

24
00:01:56.319 --> 00:02:01.163
"It's hot enough to fry an egg on the sidewalk!"

25
00:02:01.623 --> 00:02:02.484
my mom said.

26
00:02:03.444 --> 00:02:04.966
She didn't mean that, of course.

27
00:02:05.966 --> 00:02:08.569
But the sidewalk was really hot.

28
00:02:10.671 --> 00:02:13.734
When we got home, a truck was parked outside of our building.

29
00:02:14.714 --> 00:02:17.017
A sign on it read: "Elmer's Electricity.

30
00:02:17.257 --> 00:02:19.479
Stay Cool In Summer, Warm In Winter!"

31
00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:22.782
Mr. Calabria was standing near the truck.

32
00:02:25.825 --> 00:02:29.268
"The men are here to fix the electricity in the building," he told us.

33
00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:32.581
"They have to put in a lot of new wires.

34
00:02:32.901 --> 00:02:33.981
It could take a few days."

35
00:02:34.001 --> 00:02:36.802
"A few days!"

36
00:02:37.402 --> 00:02:38.303
groaned Josh.

37
00:02:38.943 --> 00:02:40.223
My mom groaned too.

38
00:02:42.924 --> 00:02:46.245
I remembered last winter when my cousin Oliver came to visit.

39
00:02:47.966 --> 00:02:51.107
The building's furnace had broken and we had no heat.

40
00:02:52.067 --> 00:02:53.688
Now we had nothing but heat!

41
00:02:55.828 --> 00:03:00.570
Since our apartment had no electricity, we had to use candles and flashlights at night.

42
00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:04.292
The candles made me feel even hotter.

43
00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:10.654
On Monday the workmen were still trying to fix the electricity.

44
00:03:11.895 --> 00:03:16.056
Mr. Chen gave all of us some money to buy ice pops at the market.

45
00:03:17.017 --> 00:03:21.859
We were sitting on the front steps, licking our ice pops, when Molly suddenly screamed.

46
00:03:21.879 --> 00:03:26.013
"Help! A bee!"

47
00:03:26.473 --> 00:03:26.973
she yelled.

48
00:03:26.993 --> 00:03:29.514
"It's going to sting me!"

49
00:03:30.655 --> 00:03:34.938
Molly jumped up and ran down the steps, trying to get away from the bee.

50
00:03:34.958 --> 00:03:38.700
"Throw away your ice pop, Molly!"

51
00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:40.040
shouted Josh.

52
00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:42.642
"Bees love sugar!"

53
00:03:42.662 --> 00:03:45.143
"That's right!"

54
00:03:45.504 --> 00:03:45.984
I cried.

55
00:03:46.004 --> 00:03:47.925
"The bee is not after you.

56
00:03:48.145 --> 00:03:49.586
It's after your ice pop!"

57
00:03:50.667 --> 00:03:53.048
But Molly didn't want to throw away her ice pop.

58
00:03:54.756 --> 00:03:57.597
She held on to it as she ran up and down the steps.

59
00:03:59.238 --> 00:04:01.899
The bee followed, buzzing all around her ice pop.

60
00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:06.281
Molly screamed and leaped down three steps at once.

61
00:04:09.062 --> 00:04:12.164
At the bottom she stumbled and fell down on the sidewalk.

62
00:04:13.084 --> 00:04:15.265
The ice pop flew out of her hand.

63
00:04:16.325 --> 00:04:19.907
The bee buzzed off and landed on Molly's ice pop.

64
00:04:20.967 --> 00:04:22.368
Molly started to cry.

65
00:04:25.986 --> 00:04:28.427
Caswell held out his ice pop.

66
00:04:28.447 --> 00:04:33.230
"Here, have some of mine," he told Molly.

67
00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:36.852
"I don't think bees like lime flavor."

68
00:04:36.873 --> 00:04:43.436
"I'm not crying about my ice pop," wailed Molly.

69
00:04:43.456 --> 00:04:45.598
"It's my foot.

70
00:04:45.978 --> 00:04:48.259
I hurt it and I can't get up!"
